# Fleet votes with callbacks days or weeks later. House style: content/STYLE.md.
# Both sides of every vote are reasonable people being reasonable.

# --- Header tank pressure ---------------------------------------------------
card dec_header
type decision
days 3 20
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave watch vent
text A sensor on {A}'s header tank reports a slow pressure rise. {A} wants to vent now. {B} wants to watch it one more day, because the trend looks like sensor drift.
option vent | Vent now | The vent is clean, and the fleet loses methane it would have liked to keep. Mission Control replies 22 minutes later: "Concur."
  set hdr_vented
  who hdr_who A
  res fuel -2
option watch | Watch it a day | The pressure levels off overnight. It was drift, from a sensor with a failing reference. {B} swaps it on the next shift and manages not to mention it for nearly an hour, a fleet record for restraint.
  set hdr_watched
  who hdr_who B
  bond A B 3

card hdr_review
type event
due
once
days 21 40
roles A
when flag hdr_vented
when is A hdr_who
text The propellant review arrives from Earth. The methane vented from {A}'s header tank is listed to three decimal places, under the heading "Prudent". {A} prints it out and tapes it to the tank access panel.
do morale A 4

card hdr_sensor
type event
due
once
days 21 40
roles A
when flag hdr_watched
when is A hdr_who
text Earth sends the teardown report on the header sensor {A} pulled: a reference resistor had cracked from launch vibration. Two more ships in the fleet carry the same batch. {A} has their replacements bagged and labelled by dinner.
do res spares -1
do morale A 4

# --- Fleet portrait -----------------------------------------------------------
card dec_photo
type decision
days 6 24
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean warm fly decline
text Public affairs wants a fleet portrait: seven ships in one frame, with Earth behind them. It costs propellant to fly the formation. The request uses the word "iconic" four times.
option fly | Fly the formation | Seven ships close to formation distance for eleven minutes. {A} takes the shot from a camera on {A}'s ship. Nobody breathes until the ships are apart again.
  set photo_taken
  res fuel -2
  morale A 4
option decline | Politely decline | The fleet sends a polite no and a very good photo of a single ship. Public affairs replies with one word: "Noted."
  set photo_declined

card photo_back
type beat
due
once
days 18 40
roles A
when flag photo_taken
when cond A ok
text The fleet portrait made the front page of every news site on Earth, 20 minutes ago. {A} zooms in and finds their own ship: a small bright dot, third from the left.
do morale A 5

# --- Water recovery -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_water
type decision
days 8 26
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave degrade strip
when cond A ok
text Water recovery on {A}'s ship is down to 93 percent from 98. {A} wants to strip the processor now. {B} wants to run it degraded and fix it when things are calmer. Out here, things don't get calmer.
option strip | Strip it now | The processor spends nine hours in pieces on the deck. {A} finds a clogged filter and a check valve installed backwards at the factory. Recovery is back to 98 percent by dinner.
  set water_fixed
  res spares -1
  trait A curious 3
option degrade | Run it degraded | The fleet goes on water rationing. Nobody complains out loud. {A} logs the recovery rate every hour, which is its own kind of complaint.
  set water_rationed
  who water_who A
  morale A -3

card water_fail
type event
due
once
days 18 40
roles A B
when flag water_rationed
when is A water_who
when apart B A
when cond B ok
text The degraded water processor on {A}'s ship quits at 04:00. {A} has the rebuild plan taped inside the panel door, already written. {B} crosses over with the spare valve, and the two of them have water flowing by breakfast.
do move B A
do bond A B 8
do res spares -1
do clr water_rationed

# --- Cargo shift (mechanical) ------------------------------------------------
card dec_cargo
type decision
days 10 30
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean warm restow trim
text A mass check shows the center of mass on {A}'s ship has moved a few centimeters. Cargo shifted on a bracket that was fine in the model. {A} wants to re-stow it all by hand. {B} suggests trimming it out with the engines and saving everyone a day of lifting.
option restow | Re-stow by hand | Eleven hours of strapping and unstrapping. The center of mass is back where the model said it would be, and the bracket gets redesigned on the spot with zip ties and spite.
  set cargo_restowed
  res spares -1
  morale A -2
  bond A B 4
option trim | Trim with engines | The engines soak up the offset, at a small propellant cost on every burn for the rest of the flight. {B} keeps a running total. It is not small.
  set cargo_trimmed
  res fuel -2

card cargo_after
type event
due
once
days 22 40
roles A
when flag cargo_restowed
when cond A ok
text During the big correction burn, the zip-tied bracket on {A}'s ship is the only mount in the bay that doesn't move a millimeter. Earth asks for the design. {A} sends a photo and the word "spite".
do morale A 4

# --- Clocks -----------------------------------------------------------------
card dec_clock
type decision
days 4 30
weight 6
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious shift keep
text Mission Control proposes moving the fleet's clocks two hours forward, to line up with the ground team's shifts. {A} is for it. {B} has seen this study before.
option shift | Change the clocks | The fleet shifts its clocks. Everyone is tired for three days and then fine, exactly as the study predicted and nobody believed.
  set clock_shifted
option keep | Keep fleet time | The fleet keeps its clocks. The ground team adjusts instead, and sends a photo of the night shift's pizza as evidence.
  set clock_kept

# --- Course correction -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_trim
type decision
days 12 28
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave now wait
text Navigation shows the fleet drifting toward the edge of the arrival corridor. {A} wants a small correction burn now. {B} wants to wait for the scheduled burn, which costs more but leaves time to check the solution three times.
option now | Burn now | A short, clean burn. {A} watches the residuals come in under a tenth of a meter per second and allows a single fist pump.
  set trim_early
  res fuel -1
option wait | Wait and check | The solution gets checked three times, then a fourth. The scheduled burn goes off on time and on target, and {B} lets the computer fly it.
  set trim_late
  res fuel -3

card trim_callback
type event
due
once
days 29 40
roles A
when fired dec_trim
when cond A ok
when trait A curious >= -10
text The final navigation fix comes in: the fleet sits within a few kilometers of the center of the arrival corridor. {A} reads the number twice, then pins it to the wall beside Earth's last decent photo.
do morale A 3

# --- Arrival: dust storm over the landing region -------------------------------
card dec_arrival
type decision
days 33 39
weight 30
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave hold wait
text Orbiters at Mars report a regional dust storm building over the landing zone. {A} wants to hold the arrival plan and trust the margins. {B} wants to burn for a longer capture orbit and wait it out, at a real cost in propellant.
option hold | Hold the plan | The arrival plan stands. {A} runs the entry numbers for the worst-case dust load and posts them where everyone can see.
  set arrive_hold
option wait | Long orbit, wait | The fleet commits to the long orbit. {B} recomputes every margin. They are thinner than anyone would like, and they are enough.
  set arrive_wait
  res fuel -4
